  "post": {
   "title": "Anthropic's junior tech hires fell from 27% to 9%: what its own report says",
   "tiktok_caption": "Anthropic says junior technical hires fell from 27% to 9% and its AI agents log six times the staff hours. But it's one company, and part of it is growth. #AI #Jobs #Anthropic #EntryLevel #FredsDesk #fyp",
   "yt_caption": "Anthropic's own employment report says the junior share of its technical hires fell from 27% to 9%, and juniors fell from 21% to 14% of technical staff. Its AI agents logged six times the staff hours. The report is descriptive and covers one company. Follow FredsDesk for daily AI",
   "pinned_comment": "Caveats: this is Anthropic reporting on itself, an AI-heavy software company, so it may not match the wider job market. The report describes the pattern and says part of it is the company's rapid growth; it does not say AI alone caused it. The six-to-one agent hours figure compares agent runtime with staff hours estimated from headcount, so it is not a count of jobs replaced. Sources: Anthropic, The Decoder, AI Weekly.",
